From: hashtagbasit
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: enable UFS MCQ

The controller supports MCQ, but without an "mcq" region ufs-qcom logs
"MCQ resource not found in device tree" and falls back to one 32-slot
doorbell queue. Add the MCQ region (UFS base + 0xe0 * 0x200, as
ufs-qcom.h has it) and the ITS MSI parent for its per-queue interrupts.

On a Pocket FIT this gives 8 I/O queues of 64 and cuts 4K random read
latency at QD1 from 158 to 117 us. Throughput is unchanged.

Same layout as Qualcomm's posted patch and eliza.dtsi.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
@@ -3985,7 +3985,10 @@
 
 		ufs_mem_hc: ufshc@1d84000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", "qcom,ufshc", "jedec,ufs-2.0";
-			reg = <0 0x01d84000 0 0x3000>;
+			reg = <0 0x01d84000 0 0x3000>,
+			      <0 0x01da0000 0 0x15000>;
+			reg-names = "std",
+				    "mcq";
 
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 265 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 
@@ -4025,6 +4028,8 @@
 
 			dma-coherent;
 
+			msi-parent = <&gic_its 0x60>;
+
 			lanes-per-direction = <2>;
 			qcom,ice = <&ice>;
 
